%
% Policy. Public documents of ISOs, RTOs, FERC, SPP, NERC, NAESB and stakeholder
% filings are tracked under sources/, and the entry's file field names the tracked
% copy. Academic papers, books and journal articles are link-only: the PDF is never
% committed, the entry carries url, and no file field. Two further kinds are link-only
% whatever their publisher: the SPP Markets+ Protocols, whose first page reads
% "Copyright 2025 by Southwest Power Pool, Inc. All rights reserved.", and the two
% September 16, 2026 workshop files, the transactions deck and the agenda deck,
% which SPP posts as members of one slide-deck zip. The local copies carry "ISO
% Internal" and "SPP Internal Only" markings, stay untracked, and each entry
% carries the url of the zip. A tracked workshop deck is the excerpt of the
% posted deck that the notebooks cite, named in the entry's note.
%
% Naming. A tracked file is <bib key>.<ext> under the folder of its category, with no
% spaces, parentheses or capitals. The workshop excerpts are the exception and
% keep date-named files under sources/workshops/, listed with their source url and
% SHA-256 in sources/workshops/manifest.json. sources/manifest.json lists every
% tracked and link-only item. sources/excerpts/<key>.md holds the passages the
% notebooks cite, each read from the source at the stated page.


